{"data":{"id":"10.3886/e112367v1","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.3886/e112367v1","prefix":"10.3886","suffix":"e112367v1","identifiers":[],"alternateIdentifiers":[],"creators":[{"name":"Bardhan, Pranab","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Pranab","familyName":"Bardhan","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Mookherjee, Dilip","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Dilip","familyName":"Mookherjee","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"lang":"en","title":"Replication data for: Determinants of Redistributive Politics: An Empirical Analysis of Land Reforms in West Bengal, India"}],"publisher":"ICPSR - Interuniversity Consortium for Political and Social Research","container":{},"publicationYear":2010,"subjects":[],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2010","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"DATA","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"dataset","schemaOrg":"Dataset","resourceTypeGeneral":"Dataset"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsSupplementTo","relatedIdentifier":"10.1257/aer.100.4.1572","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"IsDocumentedBy","relatedIdentifier":"10.1257/aer.100.4.1572","resourceTypeGeneral":"Text","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","description":"We investigate political determinants of land reform implementation in the Indian state of West Bengal. Using a village panel spanning 1974-1998, we do not find evidence supporting the hypothesis that land reforms were positively and monotonically related to control of local governments by a Left Front coalition vis-à-vis the right-centrist Congress party, combined with lack of commitment to policy platforms. Instead, the evidence is consistent with a quasi-Downsian theory stressing the role of opportunism (reelection concerns) and electoral competition. (JEL D72, O13, O17, Q15)","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"ht